Bootstrap: docker
From: continuumio/miniconda3:latest

%files
    workflow/envs/CVRCseq.yml /env.yml

%post
    conda env create -f /env.yml -n CVRCseq
    conda clean -a -y

%environment
    export PATH=/opt/conda/envs/CVRCseq/bin:$PATH
    export CONDA_DEFAULT_ENV=CVRCseq

%labels
    Author CVRCseq
    Version 1.0

%help
    CVRCseq Singularity container.
    Contains the full CVRCseq conda environment as a single portable image.

    Build — Option A: fakeroot (requires sysadmin to enable fakeroot for your account):
        srun --partition=cpu_short --mem=16G --cpus-per-task=4 --time=60 --pty bash
        module load singularity/3.11.5
        cd /gpfs/home/gildem01/workflows/CVRCseq
        singularity build --fakeroot /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif CVRCseq.def

    Build — Option B: pull from Docker Hub (no root needed; image built via GitHub Actions CI):
        module load singularity/3.11.5
        singularity pull --dir /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/ docker://mgildea87/cvrcsseq:latest
        mv /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/cvrcsseq_latest.sif /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif

    Test:
        singularity exec --bind /gpfs /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif snakemake --version
        singularity exec --bind /gpfs /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif python --version
        singularity exec --bind /gpfs /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif multiqc --version

    Run pipeline with container:
        bash workflow/scripts/snakemake_init.sh -w RNAseq_PE -d /path/to/fastq -i /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif

    Unlock if needed:
        singularity exec --bind /gpfs /gpfs/data/cvrcbioinfolab/gildem01/CVRCseq.sif snakemake --unlock --profile config/profile
